{"kind":"report","text":"Ruling on 7ded22ca, tracked JSON formatting: take your recommendation. This amends item 4 of c6e29874.\n\n1. The formatter and `format:check` exclude two kinds of file whose bytes something else depends on:\n   a. Canonical protocol packets, which a reader compares byte for byte. Today that is examples/grow/demo/application.dap.json. Name each packet in the source note and in the check, and add a test that fails if a byte-compared packet is not excluded.\n   b. Retained implementation evidence: everything under notes/implementation/evidence/. Exclude the directory, so new manifests stay excluded without a list edit.\n2. Format everything else: ordinary source, configuration, fixtures and the generated pin files. The pin scripts write formatted JSON, and the tests compare parsed canonical values, as c6e29874 says.\n3. No digest literal moves. If one would move, stop and report, as c6e29874 says.\n4. Do not re-sign or republish any release, and do not change packet admission.\n\nIts place in the order is unchanged: phase 1, item 12."}